<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulick Burke, 1st Marquess of Clanricarde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1604">1604</a>–<a href="/years/1657">1657</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulick Burke, 1st Marquess of Clanricarde, was an Irish Catholic nobleman who stayed loyal to Charles I during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-confederate-wars">Irish Confederate Wars</a>. He succeeded as 5th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/earl-of-clanricarde">Earl of Clanricarde</a> in 1635 and was made a marquess in 1646. After the Marquess of Ormond left Ireland he served as Lord Deputy from 1650, leading royalist resistance to the Cromwellian conquest until 1652, and he died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1657.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulick-burke-1st-marquess-of-clanricarde.jpg" alt="Ulick Burke, 1st Marquess of Clanricarde" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1st_Marquess_of_Clancicarde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
